            <ArticleTitle>A short non-cytotoxic antimicrobial peptide designed from Aβ29-40 adopts a nanostructure and shows in vivo anti-endotoxin activity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13079-13082</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc07547b</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aβ29-40 residues with tryptophan in place of the lone methionine residue and three arginine residues added to its C-terminus exhibited augmented antibacterial activities and protected mice against a lethal dose of LPS. The results show the conversion of a Aβ29-40 segment into a cell-selective antimicrobial/anti-endotoxin peptide with nanostructure and cation-π interaction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
